step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a robust median over the most consistent 5 models (pool1) to see if trimming improves over baseline median.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a simple inverse-error weighted average over the full pool to see if it improves on the best weighted w1 baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple best_single strategy with the strongest model ARIMA to see if single best outperforms weighted combos.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ARIMA"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean over the full pool to see if trimming the extremes improves over the current best weighted w1 baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a robust median over a slightly larger pool (pool2) to see if adding THETA improves robustness while keeping many models.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Test a DTW barycenter over the small, highly correlated pool1 to see if a robust consensus beats weighted w1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a DBA combination on the more stable pool3 to see if DTW barycenter of the best‑consistent models improves over weighted baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool3","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Try a robust median over the larger pool3 to see if expanding the model set improves robustness compared to median pool2.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool3"}

Thought: Test a weighted inverse_error combination on pool2 to see if restricting to a more stable subset improves over full‑pool weighting.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","models":["ARIMA","ETS","THETA","CWT_catboost","FT_catboost","ONLY_CWT_catboost"],"weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the smaller, high‑rank pool (pool4) using the baseline inverse‑error weight (w1) to see if restricting to the most stable models improves performance.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on pool4 using the inverse-error weight w2 to see if a different weighting improves over the current best weighted w1 pool4 strategy.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"w2"}

Thought: Try a simple mean over pool4 to see if a straightforward average can beat weighted w1 in this trend‑dominated series.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Test a DTW barycenter over pool4 to see if it beats the current mean/weighted pools.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool4","dba_max_iter":30}

